  "_read_me": "USD per million tokens. cache_write_5m / cache_write_1h = new input written to the 5-minute / 1-hour prompt cache (OpenAI: its 30-minute / 12-hour writes); cache_read = input re-read from the cache. 'over': {'above': N, ...} = the rates for a call whose prompt (new + written + re-read input) is over N tokens. 'checked': true = the rate was checked against the source below on as_of; false = a guess, shown as an estimate. Override any entry in ~/.sessioncost/prices.json (merged) or with --prices <file>.",
  "as_of": "2026-10-29",
  "source": "Checked 2026-10-29 on the vendors' own pages. Anthropic: platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing (cache writes 1.25x input for 5 minutes, 2x for 1 hour; cache reads 0.1x input, 0.05x on Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5, 0.025x on Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1; Haiku 5.5 is priced by prompt length, higher over 100,000 tokens; US-only inference costs 1.1x, not modelled). claude-opus-5-5 and claude-haiku-4-5 also cross-checked against Claude Code's own logged cost to the cent. OpenAI: developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing, Standard tier (30-minute and 12-hour cache writes are listed for GPT-6 and GPT-5.6; GPT-5.5, GPT-5.3-Codex and GPT-5.2 list none, so a write is priced as input; prompts over 272K tokens use the long-context rates; GPT-5.6 Sol has a promotional price 'at least through November 21, 2026' that the page does not state, so its listed price is used). Unlisted gpt-* / codex-* models use default-openai. Google: ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing, Standard paid tier (Gemini 3.8 and 3.6 Flash: these prices run to 2026-12-31, then double; Gemini 3.7 Flash is not listed: priced as 3.8, not checked); unlisted gemini-* models use default-gemini. Antigravity is not billed per token, so its money is always shown as API-equivalent. Cursor (cursor.com/docs/models, checked 2026-10-27): composer-2.5, Grok 4.7 and Grok 4.7 (Fast) $4 input / $1 cache read / $12 output; Cursor charges these only for use beyond its plan's allowance; long context (>256k input tokens) is billed at 2x standard rates, and 3x in Fast mode, which this table does not model. grok-4.7-medium, grok-4.7-high-fast and gemini-3.8-flash-n are not listed by those names: priced as their base model, not checked.",
